                        "entry_id": "9d300daf-240c-37a3-84de-4d062ca4d73d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The belief that priests can act as mediators between God and humankind."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0797a07e-b1e9-44da-864f-468afcf7bb28",
                                "sense_id": "d27eb7e7-b466-38ef-a101-4063a4b59ed8",
                                "text": "[T]hey tell fortunes, which practice, confined to a certain caste but forbidden to others, seems to be a kind of sacerdotalism."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "97955020-ccbe-46eb-b6b3-a41d1ab3cc51",
                                "sense_id": "d27eb7e7-b466-38ef-a101-4063a4b59ed8",
                                "text": "You make me hate Christianity, or mysticism, or Sacerdotalism, or whatever it may be called, if it’s that which has caused this deterioration in you."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4dea823f-e37d-4e74-b5a0-8bb597c90628",
                                "sense_id": "d27eb7e7-b466-38ef-a101-4063a4b59ed8",
                                "text": "This was the phrase of that interesting mystic St. Paul (Saul) of Tarsus […] who did so much to pervert and enlarge the simpler cosmopolitan fraternalism of Jesus of Nazareth […] before it was finally overwhelmed and lost in the sacrificial sacerdotalism of formal Christianity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
